course: dictionary
lesson: 9379
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word spot has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Look at the clues before you decide. Ask: what would fit here?
explain: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» Here spots are small round marks of a different colour. Spots can also be small red lumps on the skin, but the colours and the tiger tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots.» Here a spot is a particular place. Spot is also a verb: «To spot sarcasm, check whether the words fit the situation.» Here to spot means to notice or see, often when something is hard to see.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning.
fact: A spot can be a small round mark, a small red lump on the skin, or a particular place.
fact: To spot something means to notice or see it, often when it is hard to see.
fact: «A spot of» something means a small amount, as in «a spot of rain», which is British English.
fact: To check a meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» What are the spots? | a small amount | a particular place | *small round marks of a different colour | a small red lump on the skin
exercise: «Grey squirrels bury nuts in many separate spots.» What does spots mean here? | small round marks | *particular places | small red lumps on the skin | small amounts
exercise: «To spot sarcasm, check whether the words fit the situation.» What does spot mean here? | a particular place | a small round mark | *to notice or see | a small red lump on the skin
test: «Albino animals are often easier for predators to spot.» What does spot mean here? | a particular place | a small round mark | *to see or notice | a small amount
test: Mum says, «Could I have a spot of tea?» What does a spot of tea mean? | a cup with a spot on it | a big pot of tea | *a small amount of tea | a tea stain on the table
exam: A ladybird has black spots on its red back. Which meaning of spot is this? | a small red lump on the skin | to notice or see | *a small round mark of a different colour | a particular place
